#X obj 609 11 hw.rpi.spi.max7219;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 390 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Handles communication with the MAX7219 chip for 7-segment
or 8×8 LED dot matrix displays. Each display can be connected in series
with another and controlled via a single connection.;
#X text 240 153 Note: for LED dot matrix displays \, only the write_bits
and write_reg commands will work as expected.;
#X obj 230 158 cnv 1 2 30 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -260289 -1 0;
#X text 240 193 Note: the 7-segment LED display supports only this
character set: -_0123456789ABCDEFGHIJLOPSUbcdhnoqrtu;
#X obj 230 198 cnv 1 2 30 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -260289 -1 0;
#X text 240 233 Note: if the device address argument is -1 or omitted
\, the requested action is applied to all devices in the chain.;
#X text 240 288 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 313 • Status display for a patch — showing tempo \, mode
\, numeric values or short text on a 7-segment or matrix display \,
so that the state of the patch can be read without a computer screen.;
#X text 250 383 • LED matrix animations — drawing custom patterns \,
scrolling text or simple animations on the 8×8 matrix \, for example
to build a step sequencer display or a small visualizer.;
